{'vvobex6': {'name': 'Junith Eruita', 'factionKeywords': ['Adepta Sororitas'], 'keywords': ['Character', 'Epic Hero', 'Fly', 'Imperium', 'Junith Eruita', 'Mounted'], 'models': {'models': {'6a6ad6f390a72027864dc968': {'name': 'Junith Eruita', 'number': 1, 'abilities': ['The Pulpit of Saint Holline’s Basilica', 'Fiery Conviction', 'Leader', 'Acts of Faith', 'Deadly Demise 1', 'Stealth'], 'weapons': [{'name': 'Twin Ministorum Heavy Flamer', 'number': 1}, {'name': 'Mace of Castigation', 'number': 1}]}}, 'totalNumberOfModels': 1}, 'isSingleModel': True, 'uuid': 'vvobex6', 'abilities': {'The Pulpit of Saint Holline’s Basilica': {'name': 'The Pulpit of Saint Holline’s Basilica', 'desc': '\nThis unit has Stealth.\nMelee attacks that target this unit have ‑1 to hit rolls.\n'}, 'Fiery Conviction': {'name': 'Fiery Conviction', 'desc': 'If this model is on the battlefield at the start\nof your Command phase, you can choose one of the following:\n■ Discard 1 Miracle dice and gain 1CP.\n■ Take a Leadership test for this model, if that test is passed, gain 1CP.'}, 'Leader': {'name': 'Leader', 'desc': 'While a Bodyguard unit contains a Leader, it is known as an Attached unit and, with the exception of rules that are triggered when units are destroyed (pg 12), it is treated as a single unit for all rules purposes. Each time an attack targets an Attached unit, until the attacking unit has resolved all of its attacks, you must use the Toughness characteristic of the Bodyguard models in that unit, even if a Leader in that unit has a different Toughness characteristic. Each time an attack successfully wounds an Attached unit, that attack cannot be allocated to a Character model in that unit, even if that Character model has lost one or more wounds or has already had attacks allocated to it this phase. As soon as the last Bodyguard model in an Attached unit has been destroyed, any attacks made against that unit that have yet to be allocated can then be allocated to Character models in that unit.\nEach time the last model in a Bodyguard unit is destroyed, each CHARACTER unit that is part of that Attached unit becomes a separate unit, with its original Starting Strength. If this happens as the result of an attack, they become separate units after the attacking unit has resolved all of its attacks. \nEach time the last model in a CHARACTER unit that is attached to a Bodyguard unit is destroyed and there is not another CHARACTER unit attached, that Attached unit’s Bodyguard unit becomes a separate unit, with its original Starting Strength. If this happens as the result of an attack, they become separate units after the attacking unit has resolved all of its attacks. \nEach time a unit that is part of an Attached unit is destroyed, it does not have the keywords of any other units that make up that Attached unit (unless it has those keywords on its own datasheet) for the purposes of any rules that would be triggered when that unit is destroyed.'}, 'Acts of Faith': {'name': 'Acts of Faith', 'desc': 'If your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, each unit from your army with this ability can perform one Act of Faith per phase. This is done using Miracle dice.\nGAINING MIRACLE DICE\nIf your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, you gain 1 Miracle dice:\n\nAt the start of each battle round.\nEach time an Adepta Sororitas unit from your army is destroyed.\n\nEach time you gain a Miracle dice, roll one D6. The number you roll is the value of that Miracle dice. This value cannot be changed or re-rolled, unless a rule specifically states otherwise. Keep your Miracle dice to one side – this is your Miracle dice pool.\nPERFORMING AN ACT OF FAITH\nBefore making a dice roll for a model or unit from your army with the Acts of Faith ability, if you have one or more dice in your Miracle dice pool, that unit can perform an Act of Faith. If it does, select one of the dice from your Miracle dice pool to substitute that dice roll (if a roll involves more than one dice, e.g. a Charge roll or Battle-shock test, only a single dice can\nbe substituted). The dice that is being substituted is not rolled; instead the value of the selected Miracle dice is used as if it had been rolled (this counts as an unmodified dice roll of that value for all rules purposes). Each Miracle dice can only be selected for substitution once. Once all Miracle dice substitutions have been made, remove the chosen Miracle dice from your Miracle dice pool, and roll all remaining, unsubstituted dice that are a part of the dice roll. You can use Miracle dice when a unit performs an Act of Faith for any of the following types of dice roll:\n■ Advance roll\n■ Battle-shock test\n■ Charge roll\n■ Damage roll\n■ Hit roll\n■ Saving throw\n■ Wound roll'}, 'Deadly Demise 1': {'name': 'Deadly Demise 1', 'desc': 'This ability always takes the form Deadly Demise X. Each time a model in this unit is destroyed, after the units embarked within it (if any) have made their emergency disembark moves, roll one D6. On a 6, that model suffers a deadly demise; each unit within 6" of that model suffers a number of mortal wounds denoted by X (if this is a random number, roll separately for each unit within 6"). \nExample: An Impulsor with a unit of Intercessors embarked within it is destroyed by ranged attacks. First, any unresolved attacks made by the attacking unit are resolved. Then the Intercessors make an emergency disembark move. Then the roll is made for the Deadly Demise ability, and on a 6, that ability is resolved. Finally, the Impulsor is removed from the battlefield.'}, 'Stealth': {'name': 'Stealth', 'desc': 'If every model in a unit has this ability, each time a ranged attack targets that unit, that unit has the benefit of cover against that attack (13.08).'}}, 'modelProfiles': {'Junith Eruita': {'m': '8"', 't': '5', 'sv': '2+', 'w': '8', 'ld': '6+', 'oc': '2', 'insv': '4+', 'name': 'Junith Eruita'}}, 'weapons': {'Twin Ministorum Heavy Flamer': {'range': '12"', 'a': 'D6', 'bsws': 'N/A', 's': '6', 'ap': '-1', 'd': '1', 'number': 1, 'abilities': 'Ignores Cover, Torrent, Twin-Linked', 'shortAbilities': 'Ignores Cover, Torrent, Twin-Linked', 'name': 'Twin Ministorum Heavy Flamer'}, 'Mace of Castigation': {'range': 'Melee', 'a': '4', 'bsws': '2+', 's': '6', 'ap': '-2', 'd': '2', 'number': 1, 'abilities': '-', 'shortAbilities': '-', 'name': 'Mace of Castigation'}}, 'rules': [], 'unassignedWeapons': []}, 'n2cv6vr': {'name': 'Morvenn Vahl', 'factionKeywords': ['Adepta Sororitas'], 'keywords': ['Character', 'Epic Hero', 'Imperium', 'Morvenn Vahl', 'Vehicle', 'Walker', 'Warlord'], 'models': {'models': {'6a6ad6f390a72027864dc969': {'name': 'Morvenn Vahl', 'number': 1, 'abilities': ['Abbess Sanctorum', 'Righteous Repugnance', 'Leader', 'Warlord', 'Supreme Commander', 'Acts of Faith', 'Deadly Demise 1'], 'weapons': [{'name': 'Fidelis', 'number': 1}, {'name': '➤ Paragon missile launcher - prioris', 'number': 1}, {'name': '➤ Paragon missile launcher - sanctorum', 'number': 1}, {'name': '➤ Lance of Illumination - strike', 'number': 1}, {'name': '➤ Lance of Illumination - sweep', 'number': 1}]}}, 'totalNumberOfModels': 1}, 'isSingleModel': True, 'uuid': 'n2cv6vr', 'abilities': {'Abbess Sanctorum': {'name': 'Abbess Sanctorum', 'desc': 'While this model is leading a unit, each time a model in that unit makes an attack, you can re-roll the Hit roll and you can re-roll the Wound roll.'}, 'Righteous Repugnance': {'name': 'Righteous Repugnance', 'desc': "Each time this model's unit is selected to shoot or fight, you can discard 1 Miracle dice. If you do, until the end of the phase, add 3 to the Attacks characteristic of Fidelis and the Lance of Illumination. Each time an enemy unit is destroyed by this model, you gain 1 Miracle dice."}, 'Leader': {'name': 'Leader', 'desc': 'While a Bodyguard unit contains a Leader, it is known as an Attached unit and, with the exception of rules that are triggered when units are destroyed (pg 12), it is treated as a single unit for all rules purposes. Each time an attack targets an Attached unit, until the attacking unit has resolved all of its attacks, you must use the Toughness characteristic of the Bodyguard models in that unit, even if a Leader in that unit has a different Toughness characteristic. Each time an attack successfully wounds an Attached unit, that attack cannot be allocated to a Character model in that unit, even if that Character model has lost one or more wounds or has already had attacks allocated to it this phase. As soon as the last Bodyguard model in an Attached unit has been destroyed, any attacks made against that unit that have yet to be allocated can then be allocated to Character models in that unit.\nEach time the last model in a Bodyguard unit is destroyed, each CHARACTER unit that is part of that Attached unit becomes a separate unit, with its original Starting Strength. If this happens as the result of an attack, they become separate units after the attacking unit has resolved all of its attacks. \nEach time the last model in a CHARACTER unit that is attached to a Bodyguard unit is destroyed and there is not another CHARACTER unit attached, that Attached unit’s Bodyguard unit becomes a separate unit, with its original Starting Strength. If this happens as the result of an attack, they become separate units after the attacking unit has resolved all of its attacks. \nEach time a unit that is part of an Attached unit is destroyed, it does not have the keywords of any other units that make up that Attached unit (unless it has those keywords on its own datasheet) for the purposes of any rules that would be triggered when that unit is destroyed.'}, 'Supreme Commander': {'name': 'Supreme Commander', 'desc': 'If this model is in your army, it must be your WARLORD.'}, 'Acts of Faith': {'name': 'Acts of Faith', 'desc': 'If your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, each unit from your army with this ability can perform one Act of Faith per phase. This is done using Miracle dice.\nGAINING MIRACLE DICE\nIf your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, you gain 1 Miracle dice:\n\nAt the start of each battle round.\nEach time an Adepta Sororitas unit from your army is destroyed.\n\nEach time you gain a Miracle dice, roll one D6. The number you roll is the value of that Miracle dice. This value cannot be changed or re-rolled, unless a rule specifically states otherwise. Keep your Miracle dice to one side – this is your Miracle dice pool.\nPERFORMING AN ACT OF FAITH\nBefore making a dice roll for a model or unit from your army with the Acts of Faith ability, if you have one or more dice in your Miracle dice pool, that unit can perform an Act of Faith. If it does, select one of the dice from your Miracle dice pool to substitute that dice roll (if a roll involves more than one dice, e.g. a Charge roll or Battle-shock test, only a single dice can\nbe substituted). The dice that is being substituted is not rolled; instead the value of the selected Miracle dice is used as if it had been rolled (this counts as an unmodified dice roll of that value for all rules purposes). Each Miracle dice can only be selected for substitution once. Once all Miracle dice substitutions have been made, remove the chosen Miracle dice from your Miracle dice pool, and roll all remaining, unsubstituted dice that are a part of the dice roll. You can use Miracle dice when a unit performs an Act of Faith for any of the following types of dice roll:\n■ Advance roll\n■ Battle-shock test\n■ Charge roll\n■ Damage roll\n■ Hit roll\n■ Saving throw\n■ Wound roll'}, 'Deadly Demise 1': {'name': 'Deadly Demise 1', 'desc': 'This ability always takes the form Deadly Demise X. Each time a model in this unit is destroyed, after the units embarked within it (if any) have made their emergency disembark moves, roll one D6. On a 6, that model suffers a deadly demise; each unit within 6" of that model suffers a number of mortal wounds denoted by X (if this is a random number, roll separately for each unit within 6"). \nExample: An Impulsor with a unit of Intercessors embarked within it is destroyed by ranged attacks. First, any unresolved attacks made by the attacking unit are resolved. Then the Intercessors make an emergency disembark move. Then the roll is made for the Deadly Demise ability, and on a 6, that ability is resolved. Finally, the Impulsor is removed from the battlefield.'}, 'Warlord': {'name': 'Warlord', 'desc': 'The Warlord'}}, 'modelProfiles': {'Morvenn Vahl': {'m': '8"', 't': '7', 'sv': '2+', 'w': '8', 'ld': '6+', 'oc': '3', 'insv': '4+', 'name': 'Morvenn Vahl'}}, 'weapons': {'Fidelis': {'range': '36"', 'a': '3', 'bsws': '2+', 's': '6', 'ap': '-1', 'd': '2', 'number': 1, 'abilities': 'Sustained Hits 1', 'shortAbilities': 'Sustained Hits 1', 'name': 'Fidelis'}, '➤ Paragon missile launcher - prioris': {'range': '36"', 'a': '2', 'bsws': '2+', 's': '9', 'ap': '-2', 'd': 'D6', 'number': 1, 'abilities': '-', 'shortAbilities': '-', 'name': '➤ Paragon missile launcher - prioris'}, '➤ Paragon missile launcher - sanctorum': {'range': '36"', 'a': '2D6', 'bsws': '2+', 's': '4', 'ap': '0', 'd': '1', 'number': 1, 'abilities': 'Blast', 'shortAbilities': 'Blast', 'name': '➤ Paragon missile launcher - sanctorum'}, '➤ Lance of Illumination - strike': {'range': 'Melee', 'a': '5', 'bsws': '2+', 's': '8', 'ap': '-2', 'd': '3', 'number': 1, 'abilities': 'Devastating Wounds', 'shortAbilities': 'Devastating Wounds', 'name': '➤ Lance of Illumination - strike'}, '➤ Lance of Illumination - sweep': {'range': 'Melee', 'a': '10', 'bsws': '2+', 's': '5', 'ap': '-1', 'd': '1', 'number': 1, 'abilities': 'Devastating Wounds', 'shortAbilities': 'Devastating Wounds', 'name': '➤ Lance of Illumination - sweep'}}, 'rules': [], 'unassignedWeapons': []}, '755cydq': {'name': 'Saint Celestine', 'factionKeywords': ['Adepta Sororitas'], 'keywords': ['Character', 'Epic Hero', 'Fly', 'Grenades', 'Imperium', 'Infantry', 'Jump Pack', 'Saint Celestine'], 'models': {'models': {'6a6ad6f390a72027864dc96a': {'name': 'Geminae Superia', 'number': 2, 'abilities': ['Healing Tears', 'Lifewards', 'Miraculous Intervention', 'Leader', 'Acts of Faith', 'Deep Strike'], 'weapons': [{'name': 'Bolt Pistol', 'number': 1}, {'name': 'Power Weapon', 'number': 1}]}, '6a6ad6f390a72027864dc96b': {'name': 'Saint Celestine', 'number': 1, 'abilities': ['Healing Tears', 'Lifewards', 'Miraculous Intervention', 'Leader', 'Acts of Faith', 'Deep Strike'], 'weapons': [{'name': 'The Ardent Blade (ranged)', 'number': 1}, {'name': 'The Ardent Blade (melee)', 'number': 1}]}}, 'totalNumberOfModels': 3}, 'isSingleModel': False, 'uuid': '755cydq', 'abilities': {'Healing Tears': {'name': 'Healing Tears', 'desc': 'While this unit contains a Celestine model, in your Command phase, if this unit is below its Starting Strength, either one destroyed Geminae Superia model or up to D3 other Bodyguard models are returned to this unit.'}, 'Lifewards': {'name': 'Lifewards', 'desc': 'While this unit contains one or more Geminae Superia models, Celestine has the Feel No Pain 4+ ability.'}, 'Miraculous Intervention': {'name': 'Miraculous Intervention', 'desc': 'The first time this unit’s Celestine model is destroyed, roll one D6 at the end of the phase. On a 2+, set that Celestine model back up on the battlefield, as close as possible to where it was destroyed and not within Engagement Range of any enemy units, with its full wounds remaining.'}, 'Leader': {'name': 'Leader', 'desc': 'While a Bodyguard unit contains a Leader, it is known as an Attached unit and, with the exception of rules that are triggered when units are destroyed (pg 12), it is treated as a single unit for all rules purposes. Each time an attack targets an Attached unit, until the attacking unit has resolved all of its attacks, you must use the Toughness characteristic of the Bodyguard models in that unit, even if a Leader in that unit has a different Toughness characteristic. Each time an attack successfully wounds an Attached unit, that attack cannot be allocated to a Character model in that unit, even if that Character model has lost one or more wounds or has already had attacks allocated to it this phase. As soon as the last Bodyguard model in an Attached unit has been destroyed, any attacks made against that unit that have yet to be allocated can then be allocated to Character models in that unit.\nEach time the last model in a Bodyguard unit is destroyed, each CHARACTER unit that is part of that Attached unit becomes a separate unit, with its original Starting Strength. If this happens as the result of an attack, they become separate units after the attacking unit has resolved all of its attacks. \nEach time the last model in a CHARACTER unit that is attached to a Bodyguard unit is destroyed and there is not another CHARACTER unit attached, that Attached unit’s Bodyguard unit becomes a separate unit, with its original Starting Strength. If this happens as the result of an attack, they become separate units after the attacking unit has resolved all of its attacks. \nEach time a unit that is part of an Attached unit is destroyed, it does not have the keywords of any other units that make up that Attached unit (unless it has those keywords on its own datasheet) for the purposes of any rules that would be triggered when that unit is destroyed.'}, 'Acts of Faith': {'name': 'Acts of Faith', 'desc': 'If your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, each unit from your army with this ability can perform one Act of Faith per phase. This is done using Miracle dice.\nGAINING MIRACLE DICE\nIf your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, you gain 1 Miracle dice:\n\nAt the start of each battle round.\nEach time an Adepta Sororitas unit from your army is destroyed.\n\nEach time you gain a Miracle dice, roll one D6. The number you roll is the value of that Miracle dice. This value cannot be changed or re-rolled, unless a rule specifically states otherwise. Keep your Miracle dice to one side – this is your Miracle dice pool.\nPERFORMING AN ACT OF FAITH\nBefore making a dice roll for a model or unit from your army with the Acts of Faith ability, if you have one or more dice in your Miracle dice pool, that unit can perform an Act of Faith. If it does, select one of the dice from your Miracle dice pool to substitute that dice roll (if a roll involves more than one dice, e.g. a Charge roll or Battle-shock test, only a single dice can\nbe substituted). The dice that is being substituted is not rolled; instead the value of the selected Miracle dice is used as if it had been rolled (this counts as an unmodified dice roll of that value for all rules purposes). Each Miracle dice can only be selected for substitution once. Once all Miracle dice substitutions have been made, remove the chosen Miracle dice from your Miracle dice pool, and roll all remaining, unsubstituted dice that are a part of the dice roll. You can use Miracle dice when a unit performs an Act of Faith for any of the following types of dice roll:\n■ Advance roll\n■ Battle-shock test\n■ Charge roll\n■ Damage roll\n■ Hit roll\n■ Saving throw\n■ Wound roll'}, 'Deep Strike': {'name': 'Deep Strike', 'desc': 'Each time this unit makes an ingress move (20.04), if every model in this unit has this ability, it can be set up anywhere on the battlefield that is more than 8" horizontally from all enemy units, even if that is within your opponent’s deployment zone.'}}, 'modelProfiles': {'Geminae Superia': {'m': '12"', 't': '3', 'sv': '2+', 'w': '2', 'ld': '7+', 'oc': '1', 'insv': '4+', 'name': 'Geminae Superia'}, 'Saint Celestine': {'m': '12"', 't': '3', 'sv': '2+', 'w': '5', 'ld': '6+', 'oc': '1', 'insv': '4+', 'name': 'Saint Celestine'}}, 'weapons': {'Bolt Pistol': {'range': '12"', 'a': '1', 'bsws': '3+', 's': '4', 'ap': '0', 'd': '1', 'number': 1, 'abilities': 'Pistol', 'shortAbilities': 'Pistol', 'name': 'Bolt Pistol'}, 'The Ardent Blade (ranged)': {'range': '12"', 'a': 'D6', 'bsws': 'N/A', 's': '6', 'ap': '-2', 'd': '1', 'number': 1, 'abilities': 'Ignores Cover, Torrent', 'shortAbilities': 'Ignores Cover, Torrent', 'name': 'The Ardent Blade (ranged)'}, 'Power Weapon': {'range': 'Melee', 'a': '4', 'bsws': '3+', 's': '4', 'ap': '-2', 'd': '1', 'number': 1, 'abilities': '-', 'shortAbilities': '-', 'name': 'Power Weapon'}, 'The Ardent Blade (melee)': {'range': 'Melee', 'a': '5', 'bsws': '2+', 's': '6', 'ap': '-3', 'd': '2', 'number': 1, 'abilities': 'Devastating Wounds', 'shortAbilities': 'Devastating Wounds', 'name': 'The Ardent Blade (melee)'}}, 'rules': [], 'unassignedWeapons': []}, 'kymubg': {'name': 'Canoness', 'factionKeywords': ['Adepta Sororitas'], 'keywords': ['Canoness', 'Character', 'Grenades', 'Infantry'], 'models': {'models': {'6a6ad6f390a72027864dc96c': {'name': 'Canoness', 'number': 1, 'abilities': ["The Emperor's Grace", 'Sacred Command', 'Leader', 'Acts of Faith'], 'weapons': [{'name': 'Bolt Pistol', 'number': 1}, {'name': 'Blessed blade', 'number': 1}]}}, 'totalNumberOfModels': 1}, 'isSingleModel': True, 'uuid': 'kymubg', 'abilities': {"The Emperor's Grace": {'name': "The Emperor's Grace", 'desc': 'Once per battle, at the start of any phase, this model can use this ability. If it does, until the end of the phase, this model has a 2+ invulnerable save.'}, 'Sacred Command': {'name': 'Sacred Command', 'desc': 'Once per battle round, one unit from your army with this ability can use it when its unit is targeted with a Stratagem. If it does, reduce the CP cost of that use of that Stratagem by 1CP.'}, 'Leader': {'name': 'Leader', 'desc': 'While a Bodyguard unit contains a Leader, it is known as an Attached unit and, with the exception of rules that are triggered when units are destroyed (pg 12), it is treated as a single unit for all rules purposes. Each time an attack targets an Attached unit, until the attacking unit has resolved all of its attacks, you must use the Toughness characteristic of the Bodyguard models in that unit, even if a Leader in that unit has a different Toughness characteristic. Each time an attack successfully wounds an Attached unit, that attack cannot be allocated to a Character model in that unit, even if that Character model has lost one or more wounds or has already had attacks allocated to it this phase. As soon as the last Bodyguard model in an Attached unit has been destroyed, any attacks made against that unit that have yet to be allocated can then be allocated to Character models in that unit.\nEach time the last model in a Bodyguard unit is destroyed, each CHARACTER unit that is part of that Attached unit becomes a separate unit, with its original Starting Strength. If this happens as the result of an attack, they become separate units after the attacking unit has resolved all of its attacks. \nEach time the last model in a CHARACTER unit that is attached to a Bodyguard unit is destroyed and there is not another CHARACTER unit attached, that Attached unit’s Bodyguard unit becomes a separate unit, with its original Starting Strength. If this happens as the result of an attack, they become separate units after the attacking unit has resolved all of its attacks. \nEach time a unit that is part of an Attached unit is destroyed, it does not have the keywords of any other units that make up that Attached unit (unless it has those keywords on its own datasheet) for the purposes of any rules that would be triggered when that unit is destroyed.'}, 'Acts of Faith': {'name': 'Acts of Faith', 'desc': 'If your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, each unit from your army with this ability can perform one Act of Faith per phase. This is done using Miracle dice.\nGAINING MIRACLE DICE\nIf your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, you gain 1 Miracle dice:\n\nAt the start of each battle round.\nEach time an Adepta Sororitas unit from your army is destroyed.\n\nEach time you gain a Miracle dice, roll one D6. The number you roll is the value of that Miracle dice. This value cannot be changed or re-rolled, unless a rule specifically states othe