 Pack', 'number': 1, 'abilities': ['Divine Deliverance', 'Sacred Command', 'Condemnatory Psalms', 'Leader', 'Acts of Faith', 'Deep Strike'], 'weapons': [{'name': 'Blessed Halberd', 'number': 1}]}}, 'totalNumberOfModels': 1}, 'isSingleModel': True, 'uuid': '3y5zjks', 'abilities': {'Divine Deliverance': {'name': 'Divine Deliverance', 'desc': 'Once per battle, at the start of the Fight phase, this model can use this ability. If it does, until the end of the phase, add 3 to the Attacks characteristic of melee weapons equipped by the model and those weapons have the [DEVASTATING WOUNDS] ability'}, 'Sacred Command': {'name': 'Sacred Command', 'desc': 'Once per battle round, one unit from your army with this ability can use it when its unit is targeted with a Stratagem. If it does, reduce the CP cost of that use of that Stratagem by 1CP.'}, 'Condemnatory Psalms': {'name': 'Condemnatory Psalms', 'desc': 'In your Shooting phase, this unit can select one visible enemy unit within 12". That enemy unit is condemned:\n\nWhile a unit is condemned, that unit has +3" detection range.\n'}, 'Leader': {'name': 'Leader', 'desc': 'While a Bodyguard unit contains a Leader, it is known as an Attached unit and, with the exception of rules that are triggered when units are destroyed (pg 12), it is treated as a single unit for all rules purposes. Each time an attack targets an Attached unit, until the attacking unit has resolved all of its attacks, you must use the Toughness characteristic of the Bodyguard models in that unit, even if a Leader in that unit has a different Toughness characteristic. Each time an attack successfully wounds an Attached unit, that attack cannot be allocated to a Character model in that unit, even if that Character model has lost one or more wounds or has already had attacks allocated to it this phase. As soon as the last Bodyguard model in an Attached unit has been destroyed, any attacks made against that unit that have yet to be allocated can then be allocated to Character models in that unit.\nEach time the last model in a Bodyguard unit is destroyed, each CHARACTER unit that is part of that Attached unit becomes a separate unit, with its original Starting Strength. If this happens as the result of an attack, they become separate units after the attacking unit has resolved all of its attacks. \nEach time the last model in a CHARACTER unit that is attached to a Bodyguard unit is destroyed and there is not another CHARACTER unit attached, that Attached unit’s Bodyguard unit becomes a separate unit, with its original Starting Strength. If this happens as the result of an attack, they become separate units after the attacking unit has resolved all of its attacks. \nEach time a unit that is part of an Attached unit is destroyed, it does not have the keywords of any other units that make up that Attached unit (unless it has those keywords on its own datasheet) for the purposes of any rules that would be triggered when that unit is destroyed.'}, 'Acts of Faith': {'name': 'Acts of Faith', 'desc': 'If your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, each unit from your army with this ability can perform one Act of Faith per phase. This is done using Miracle dice.\nGAINING MIRACLE DICE\nIf your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, you gain 1 Miracle dice:\n\nAt the start of each battle round.\nEach time an Adepta Sororitas unit from your army is destroyed.\n\nEach time you gain a Miracle dice, roll one D6. The number you roll is the value of that Miracle dice. This value cannot be changed or re-rolled, unless a rule specifically states otherwise. Keep your Miracle dice to one side – this is your Miracle dice pool.\nPERFORMING AN ACT OF FAITH\nBefore making a dice roll for a model or unit from your army with the Acts of Faith ability, if you have one or more dice in your Miracle dice pool, that unit can perform an Act of Faith. If it does, select one of the dice from your Miracle dice pool to substitute that dice roll (if a roll involves more than one dice, e.g. a Charge roll or Battle-shock test, only a single dice can\nbe substituted). The dice that is being substituted is not rolled; instead the value of the selected Miracle dice is used as if it had been rolled (this counts as an unmodified dice roll of that value for all rules purposes). Each Miracle dice can only be selected for substitution once. Once all Miracle dice substitutions have been made, remove the chosen Miracle dice from your Miracle dice pool, and roll all remaining, unsubstituted dice that are a part of the dice roll. You can use Miracle dice when a unit performs an Act of Faith for any of the following types of dice roll:\n■ Advance roll\n■ Battle-shock test\n■ Charge roll\n■ Damage roll\n■ Hit roll\n■ Saving throw\n■ Wound roll'}, 'Deep Strike': {'name': 'Deep Strike', 'desc': 'Each time this unit makes an ingress move (20.04), if every model in this unit has this ability, it can be set up anywhere on the battlefield that is more than 8" horizontally from all enemy units, even if that is within your opponent’s deployment zone.'}}, 'modelProfiles': {'Canoness with Jump Pack': {'m': '12"', 't': '3', 'sv': '3+', 'w': '3', 'ld': '7+', 'oc': '1', 'insv': '4+', 'name': 'Canoness with Jump Pack'}}, 'weapons': {'Blessed Halberd': {'range': 'Melee', 'a': '5', 'bsws': '2+', 's': '5', 'ap': '-2', 'd': '2', 'number': 1, 'abilities': '-', 'shortAbilities': '-', 'name': 'Blessed Halberd'}}, 'rules': [], 'unassignedWeapons': []}, 'p9xlhi': {'name': 'Dialogus', 'factionKeywords': ['Adepta Sororitas'], 'keywords': ['Character', 'Dialogus', 'Imperium', 'Infantry'], 'models': {'models': {'6a6ad6f390a72027864dc96e': {'name': 'Dialogus', 'number': 1, 'abilities': ['Laud Hailer', 'Stirring Rhetoric', 'Support', 'Acts of Faith'], 'weapons': [{'name': 'Bolt pistol', 'number': 1}, {'name': 'Dialogus staff', 'number': 1}]}}, 'totalNumberOfModels': 1}, 'isSingleModel': True, 'uuid': 'p9xlhi', 'abilities': {'Laud Hailer': {'name': 'Laud Hailer', 'desc': 'Once per battle, at the start of any phase, you can select one friendly Adepta Sororitas unit that is Battle-shocked and within 12" of this model. That unit is no longer Battle-shocked.'}, 'Stirring Rhetoric': {'name': 'Stirring Rhetoric', 'desc': 'While this model is leading a unit, each time that unit performs an Act of Faith, the value of one of the Miracle dice used in that Act of Faith is first changed to a 6.'}, 'Support': {'name': 'Support', 'desc': ''}, 'Acts of Faith': {'name': 'Acts of Faith', 'desc': 'If your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, each unit from your army with this ability can perform one Act of Faith per phase. This is done using Miracle dice.\nGAINING MIRACLE DICE\nIf your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, you gain 1 Miracle dice:\n\nAt the start of each battle round.\nEach time an Adepta Sororitas unit from your army is destroyed.\n\nEach time you gain a Miracle dice, roll one D6. The number you roll is the value of that Miracle dice. This value cannot be changed or re-rolled, unless a rule specifically states otherwise. Keep your Miracle dice to one side – this is your Miracle dice pool.\nPERFORMING AN ACT OF FAITH\nBefore making a dice roll for a model or unit from your army with the Acts of Faith ability, if you have one or more dice in your Miracle dice pool, that unit can perform an Act of Faith. If it does, select one of the dice from your Miracle dice pool to substitute that dice roll (if a roll involves more than one dice, e.g. a Charge roll or Battle-shock test, only a single dice can\nbe substituted). The dice that is being substituted is not rolled; instead the value of the selected Miracle dice is used as if it had been rolled (this counts as an unmodified dice roll of that value for all rules purposes). Each Miracle dice can only be selected for substitution once. Once all Miracle dice substitutions have been made, remove the chosen Miracle dice from your Miracle dice pool, and roll all remaining, unsubstituted dice that are a part of the dice roll. You can use Miracle dice when a unit performs an Act of Faith for any of the following types of dice roll:\n■ Advance roll\n■ Battle-shock test\n■ Charge roll\n■ Damage roll\n■ Hit roll\n■ Saving throw\n■ Wound roll'}}, 'modelProfiles': {'Dialogus': {'m': '6"', 't': '3', 'sv': '3+', 'w': '3', 'ld': '6+', 'oc': '1', 'insv': '4+', 'name': 'Dialogus'}}, 'weapons': {'Bolt pistol': {'range': '12"', 'a': '1', 'bsws': '3+', 's': '4', 'ap': '0', 'd': '1', 'number': 1, 'abilities': 'Pistol', 'shortAbilities': 'Pistol', 'name': 'Bolt pistol'}, 'Dialogus staff': {'range': 'Melee', 'a': '3', 'bsws': '4+', 's': '4', 'ap': '0', 'd': '1', 'number': 1, 'abilities': '-', 'shortAbilities': '-', 'name': 'Dialogus staff'}}, 'rules': [], 'unassignedWeapons': []}, 'ux004h': {'name': 'Hospitaller', 'factionKeywords': ['Adepta Sororitas'], 'keywords': ['Character', 'Hospitaller', 'Imperium', 'Infantry'], 'models': {'models': {'6a6ad6f390a72027864dc96f': {'name': 'Hospitaller', 'number': 1, 'abilities': ['Medicus Ministorum', 'Sacred Healing', 'Support', 'Acts of Faith'], 'weapons': [{'name': 'Bolt pistol', 'number': 1}, {'name': "Chirugeon's tools", 'number': 1}]}}, 'totalNumberOfModels': 1}, 'isSingleModel': True, 'uuid': 'ux004h', 'abilities': {'Medicus Ministorum': {'name': 'Medicus Ministorum', 'desc': 'While this model is leading a unit, models in that unit have the Feel No Pain 5+ ability.'}, 'Sacred Healing': {'name': 'Sacred Healing', 'desc': 'While this model is leading a unit, in your Command phase, you can return up to 1 destroyed model (excluding Character models) to that unit. If you wish, you first discard 1 Miracle dice; if you do, you can return up to D3+1 destroyed models (excluding Character models) to that unit instead.'}, 'Support': {'name': 'Support', 'desc': ''}, 'Acts of Faith': {'name': 'Acts of Faith', 'desc': 'If your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, each unit from your army with this ability can perform one Act of Faith per phase. This is done using Miracle dice.\nGAINING MIRACLE DICE\nIf your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, you gain 1 Miracle dice:\n\nAt the start of each battle round.\nEach time an Adepta Sororitas unit from your army is destroyed.\n\nEach time you gain a Miracle dice, roll one D6. The number you roll is the value of that Miracle dice. This value cannot be changed or re-rolled, unless a rule specifically states otherwise. Keep your Miracle dice to one side – this is your Miracle dice pool.\nPERFORMING AN ACT OF FAITH\nBefore making a dice roll for a model or unit from your army with the Acts of Faith ability, if you have one or more dice in your Miracle dice pool, that unit can perform an Act of Faith. If it does, select one of the dice from your Miracle dice pool to substitute that dice roll (if a roll involves more than one dice, e.g. a Charge roll or Battle-shock test, only a single dice can\nbe substituted). The dice that is being substituted is not rolled; instead the value of the selected Miracle dice is used as if it had been rolled (this counts as an unmodified dice roll of that value for all rules purposes). Each Miracle dice can only be selected for substitution once. Once all Miracle dice substitutions have been made, remove the chosen Miracle dice from your Miracle dice pool, and roll all remaining, unsubstituted dice that are a part of the dice roll. You can use Miracle dice when a unit performs an Act of Faith for any of the following types of dice roll:\n■ Advance roll\n■ Battle-shock test\n■ Charge roll\n■ Damage roll\n■ Hit roll\n■ Saving throw\n■ Wound roll'}}, 'modelProfiles': {'Hospitaller': {'m': '6"', 't': '3', 'sv': '3+', 'w': '3', 'ld': '7+', 'oc': '1', 'insv': '6+', 'name': 'Hospitaller'}}, 'weapons': {'Bolt pistol': {'range': '12"', 'a': '1', 'bsws': '3+', 's': '4', 'ap': '0', 'd': '1', 'number': 1, 'abilities': 'Pistol', 'shortAbilities': 'Pistol', 'name': 'Bolt pistol'}, "Chirugeon's tools": {'range': 'Melee', 'a': '3', 'bsws': '4+', 's': '3', 'ap': '0', 'd': '1', 'number': 1, 'abilities': '-', 'shortAbilities': '-', 'name': "Chirugeon's tools"}}, 'rules': [], 'unassignedWeapons': []}, 'n0slwf': {'name': 'Palatine', 'factionKeywords': ['Adepta Sororitas'], 'keywords': ['Character', 'Grenades', 'Imperium', 'Infantry', 'Palatine'], 'models': {'models': {'6a6ad6f390a72027864dc970': {'name': 'Palatine', 'number': 1, 'abilities': ['Fury of the Righteous', 'Rapturous Blows', 'Leader', 'Litanies of Faith', 'Acts of Faith'], 'weapons': [{'name': 'Bolt pistol', 'number': 1}, {'name': 'Palatine blade', 'number': 1}]}}, 'totalNumberOfModels': 1}, 'isSingleModel': True, 'uuid': 'n0slwf', 'abilities': {'Fury of the Righteous': {'name': 'Fury of the Righteous', 'desc': 'While this model is leading a unit, weapons equipped by models in that unit have the [LETHAL HITS] ability.'}, 'Rapturous Blows': {'name': 'Rapturous Blows', 'desc': 'Each time this model’s unit is selected to fight, you can discard 1 Miracle dice. If you do, then until the end of the phase, each time a melee attack made by this model scores a wound, the target of that attack suffers 1 mortal wound in addition to any normal damage.'}, 'Leader': {'name': 'Leader', 'desc': 'While a Bodyguard unit contains a Leader, it is known as an Attached unit and, with the exception of rules that are triggered when units are destroyed (pg 12), it is treated as a single unit for all rules purposes. Each time an attack targets an Attached unit, until the attacking unit has resolved all of its attacks, you must use the Toughness characteristic of the Bodyguard models in that unit, even if a Leader in that unit has a different Toughness characteristic. Each time an attack successfully wounds an Attached unit, that attack cannot be allocated to a Character model in that unit, even if that Character model has lost one or more wounds or has already had attacks allocated to it this phase. As soon as the last Bodyguard model in an Attached unit has been destroyed, any attacks made against that unit that have yet to be allocated can then be allocated to Character models in that unit.\nEach time the last model in a Bodyguard unit is destroyed, each CHARACTER unit that is part of that Attached unit becomes a separate unit, with its original Starting Strength. If this happens as the result of an attack, they become separate units after the attacking unit has resolved all of its attacks. \nEach time the last model in a CHARACTER unit that is attached to a Bodyguard unit is destroyed and there is not another CHARACTER unit attached, that Attached unit’s Bodyguard unit becomes a separate unit, with its original Starting Strength. If this happens as the result of an attack, they become separate units after the attacking unit has resolved all of its attacks. \nEach time a unit that is part of an Attached unit is destroyed, it does not have the keywords of any other units that make up that Attached unit (unless it has those keywords on its own datasheet) for the purposes of any rules that would be triggered when that unit is destroyed.'}, 'Acts of Faith': {'name': 'Acts of Faith', 'desc': 'If your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, each unit from your army with this ability can perform one Act of Faith per phase. This is done using Miracle dice.\nGAINING MIRACLE DICE\nIf your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, you gain 1 Miracle dice:\n\nAt the start of each battle round.\nEach time an Adepta Sororitas unit from your army is destroyed.\n\nEach time you gain a Miracle dice, roll one D6. The number you roll is the value of that Miracle dice. This value cannot be changed or re-rolled, unless a rule specifically states otherwise. Keep your Miracle dice to one side – this is your Miracle dice pool.\nPERFORMING AN ACT OF FAITH\nBefore making a dice roll for a model or unit from your army with the Acts of Faith ability, if you have one or more dice in your Miracle dice pool, that unit can perform an Act of Faith. If it does, select one of the dice from your Miracle dice pool to substitute that dice roll (if a roll involves more than one dice, e.g. a Charge roll or Battle-shock test, only a single dice can\nbe substituted). The dice that is being substituted is not rolled; instead the value of the selected Miracle dice is used as if it had been rolled (this counts as an unmodified dice roll of that value for all rules purposes). Each Miracle dice can only be selected for substitution once. Once all Miracle dice substitutions have been made, remove the chosen Miracle dice from your Miracle dice pool, and roll all remaining, unsubstituted dice that are a part of the dice roll. You can use Miracle dice when a unit performs an Act of Faith for any of the following types of dice roll:\n■ Advance roll\n■ Battle-shock test\n■ Charge roll\n■ Damage roll\n■ Hit roll\n■ Saving throw\n■ Wound roll'}, 'Litanies of Faith': {'name': 'Litanies of Faith', 'desc': 'CANONESS or PALATINE model only. At the start of your Command phase, if the bearer is on the battlefield, take a Leadership test for the bearer. If that test is passed, you gain 1 Miracle dice.'}}, 'modelProfiles': {'Palatine': {'m': '6"', 't': '3', 'sv': '3+', 'w': '4', 'ld': '7+', 'oc': '1', 'insv': '4+', 'name': 'Palatine'}}, 'weapons': {'Bolt pistol': {'range': '12"', 'a': '1', 'bsws': '2+', 's': '4', 'ap': '0', 'd': '1', 'number': 1, 'abilities': 'Pistol', 'shortAbilities': 'Pistol', 'name': 'Bolt pistol'}, 'Palatine blade': {'range': 'Melee', 'a': '4', 'bsws': '2+', 's': '4', 'ap': '-2', 'd': '2', 'number': 1, 'abilities': '-', 'shortAbilities': '-', 'name': 'Palatine blade'}}, 'rules': [], 'unassignedWeapons': []}, 'u7g29k5': {'name': 'Battle Sisters Squad', 'factionKeywords': ['Adepta Sororitas'], 'keywords': ['Battle Sisters Squad', 'Battleline', 'Grenades', 'Imperium', 'Infantry'], 'models': {'models': {'6a6ad6f390a72027864dc971': {'name': 'Sister Superior', 'number': 1, 'abilities': ['Defenders of the Faith', 'Cherub', 'Acts of Faith'], 'weapons': [{'name': 'Bolt pistol', 'number': 1}, {'name': 'Combi-weapon', 'number': 1}, {'name': 'Close combat weapon', 'number': 1}, {'name': 'Power weapon', 'number': 1}]}, '6a6ad6f390a72027864dc972': {'name': 'Battle Sister', 'number': 6, 'abilities': ['Defenders of the Faith', 'Cherub', 'Acts of Faith'], 'weapons': [{'name': 'Bolt pistol', 'number': 1}, {'name': 'Boltgun', 'number': 1}, {'name': 'Close combat weapon', 'number': 1}]}, '6a6ad6f390a72027864dc973': {'name': 'Battle Sister w/ Simulacrum Imperialis', 'number': 1, 'abilities': ['Simulacrum Imperialis', 'Defenders of the Faith', 'Cherub', 'Acts of Faith'], 'weapons': [{'name': 'Bolt pistol', 'number': 1}, {'name': 'Boltgun', 'number': 1}, {'name': 'Close combat weapon', 'number': 1}]}, '6a6ad6f390a72027864dc974': {'name': 'Battle Sister w/ Special or Heavy Weapon', 'number': 1, 'abilities': ['Defenders of the Faith', 'Cherub', 'Acts of Faith'], 'weapons': [{'name': 'Bolt pistol', 'number': 1}, {'name': 'Multi-melta', 'number': 1}, {'name': 'Close combat weapon', 'number': 1}]}, '6a6ad6f390a72027864dc975': {'name': 'Battle Sister w/ Special Weapon', 'number': 1, 'abilities': ['Defenders of the Faith', 'Cherub', 'Acts of Faith'], 'weapons': [{'name': 'Bolt pistol', 'number': 1}, {'name': 'Meltagun', 'number': 1}, {'name': 'Close combat weapon', 'number': 1}]}}, 'totalNumberOfModels': 10}, 'isSingleModel': False, 'uuid': 'u7g29k5', 'abilities': {'Defenders of the Faith': {'name': 'Defenders of the Faith', 'desc': 'At the end of your Command phase, if this unit is within range of an objective marker you control, that objective marker remains under your control, even if you have no models within range of it, until your opponent controls it at the start or end of any turn.'}, 'Cherub': {'name': 'Cherub', 'desc': 'Once per battle, after this unit has performed an Act of Faith, you gain 1 Miracle dice.'}, 'Acts of Faith': {'name': 'Acts of Faith', 'desc': 'If your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, each unit from your army with this ability can perform one Act of Faith per phase. This is done using Miracle dice.\nGAINING MIRACLE DICE\nIf your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, you gain 1 Miracle dice:\n\nAt the start of each battle round.\nEach time an Adepta Sororitas unit from your army is destroyed.\n\nEach time you gain a Miracle dice, roll one D6. The number you roll is the value of that Miracle dice. This value cannot be changed or re-rolled, unless a rule specifically states otherwise. Keep your Miracle dice to one side – this is your Miracle dice pool.\nPERFORMING AN ACT OF FAITH\nBefore making a dice roll for a model or unit from your army with the Acts of Faith ability, if you have one or more dice in your Miracle dice pool, that unit can perform an Act of Faith. If it does, select one of the dice from your Miracle dice pool to substitute that dice roll (if a roll involves more than one dice, e.g. a Charge roll or Battle-shock test, only a single dice can\nbe substituted). The dice that is being substituted is not rolled; instead the value of the selected Miracle dice is used as if it had been rolled (this counts as an unmodified dice roll of that value for all rules purposes). Each Miracle dice can only be selected for substitution once. Once all Miracle dice substitutions have been made, remove the chosen Miracle dice from your Miracle dice pool, and roll all remaining, unsubstituted dice that are a part of the dice roll. You can use Miracle dice when a unit performs an Act of Faith for any of the following types of dice roll:\n■ Advance roll\n■ Battle-shock test\n■ Charge roll\n■ Damage roll\n■ Hit roll\n■ Saving throw\n■ Wound roll'}, 'Simulacrum Imperialis': {'name': 'Simulacrum Imperialis', 'desc': 'At the end of your Command phase, for each objective marker you control that has one or more units from your army with this ability within range of it, roll one D6: on a 4+, you gain 1 Miracle dice showing a value equal to that result.'}}, 'modelProfiles': {'Battle Sister': {'m': '6"', 't': '3', 'sv':