an make a Normal move of up to 6". If it does, until the end of the turn, this unit is not eligible to declare a charge.'}, 'Condemnatory Psalms': {'name': 'Condemnatory Psalms', 'desc': 'In your Shooting phase, this unit can select one visible enemy unit within 12". That enemy unit is condemned:\n\nWhile a unit is condemned, that unit has +3" detection range.\n'}, 'Acts of Faith': {'name': 'Acts of Faith', 'desc': 'If your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, each unit from your army with this ability can perform one Act of Faith per phase. This is done using Miracle dice.\nGAINING MIRACLE DICE\nIf your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, you gain 1 Miracle dice:\n\nAt the start of each battle round.\nEach time an Adepta Sororitas unit from your army is destroyed.\n\nEach time you gain a Miracle dice, roll one D6. The number you roll is the value of that Miracle dice. This value cannot be changed or re-rolled, unless a rule specifically states otherwise. Keep your Miracle dice to one side – this is your Miracle dice pool.\nPERFORMING AN ACT OF FAITH\nBefore making a dice roll for a model or unit from your army with the Acts of Faith ability, if you have one or more dice in your Miracle dice pool, that unit can perform an Act of Faith. If it does, select one of the dice from your Miracle dice pool to substitute that dice roll (if a roll involves more than one dice, e.g. a Charge roll or Battle-shock test, only a single dice can\nbe substituted). The dice that is being substituted is not rolled; instead the value of the selected Miracle dice is used as if it had been rolled (this counts as an unmodified dice roll of that value for all rules purposes). Each Miracle dice can only be selected for substitution once. Once all Miracle dice substitutions have been made, remove the chosen Miracle dice from your Miracle dice pool, and roll all remaining, unsubstituted dice that are a part of the dice roll. You can use Miracle dice when a unit performs an Act of Faith for any of the following types of dice roll:\n■ Advance roll\n■ Battle-shock test\n■ Charge roll\n■ Damage roll\n■ Hit roll\n■ Saving throw\n■ Wound roll'}, 'Deep Strike': {'name': 'Deep Strike', 'desc': 'Each time this unit makes an ingress move (20.04), if every model in this unit has this ability, it can be set up anywhere on the battlefield that is more than 8" horizontally from all enemy units, even if that is within your opponent’s deployment zone.'}}, 'modelProfiles': {'Seraphim Superior': {'m': '12"', 't': '3', 'sv': '3+', 'w': '1', 'ld': '7+', 'oc': '1', 'insv': '5+', 'name': 'Seraphim Superior'}, 'Seraphim': {'m': '12"', 't': '3', 'sv': '3+', 'w': '1', 'ld': '7+', 'oc': '1', 'insv': '5+', 'name': 'Seraphim'}}, 'weapons': {'Bolt pistol': {'range': '12"', 'a': '1', 'bsws': '3+', 's': '4', 'ap': '0', 'd': '1', 'number': 1, 'abilities': 'Pistol', 'shortAbilities': 'Pistol', 'name': 'Bolt pistol'}, 'Inferno Pistol': {'range': '6"', 'a': '1', 'bsws': '3+', 's': '8', 'ap': '-4', 'd': 'D3', 'number': 1, 'abilities': 'Melta 2, Pistol', 'shortAbilities': 'Melta 2, Pistol', 'name': 'Inferno Pistol'}, 'Close combat weapon': {'range': 'Melee', 'a': '2', 'bsws': '3+', 's': '3', 'ap': '0', 'd': '1', 'number': 1, 'abilities': '-', 'shortAbilities': '-', 'name': 'Close combat weapon'}}, 'rules': [], 'unassignedWeapons': []}, 'z19hc0c': {'name': 'Exorcist', 'factionKeywords': ['Adepta Sororitas'], 'keywords': ['Exorcist', 'Frame', 'Imperium', 'Smoke', 'Vehicle'], 'models': {'models': {'6a6ad6f390a72027864dc985': {'name': 'Exorcist', 'number': 1, 'abilities': ['Damaged: 1-4 Wounds Remaining', 'Devastating Refrain', 'Symphonic Payload', 'Acts of Faith', 'Deadly Demise D3'], 'weapons': [{'name': 'Heavy Bolter', 'number': 1}, {'name': 'Exorcist Missile Launcher', 'number': 1}, {'name': 'Armoured tracks', 'number': 1}]}}, 'totalNumberOfModels': 1}, 'isSingleModel': True, 'uuid': 'z19hc0c', 'abilities': {'Damaged: 1-4 Wounds Remaining': {'name': 'Damaged: 1-4 Wounds Remaining', 'desc': 'While this model has 1-4 wounds remaining, each time this model makes an attack, subtract 1 from the Hit roll.'}, 'Devastating Refrain': {'name': 'Devastating Refrain', 'desc': "In your Shooting phase, after this model has shot, if one or more of those attacks made with an Indirect Fire weapon scored a hit against an enemy unit, that unit must take a Battle-shock test. Each time such an attack destroys an enemy model that has the Deadly Demise ability, the model's Deadly Demise ability inflicts mortal wounds on a D6 roll of 5+ instead of a 6."}, 'Acts of Faith': {'name': 'Acts of Faith', 'desc': 'If your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, each unit from your army with this ability can perform one Act of Faith per phase. This is done using Miracle dice.\nGAINING MIRACLE DICE\nIf your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, you gain 1 Miracle dice:\n\nAt the start of each battle round.\nEach time an Adepta Sororitas unit from your army is destroyed.\n\nEach time you gain a Miracle dice, roll one D6. The number you roll is the value of that Miracle dice. This value cannot be changed or re-rolled, unless a rule specifically states otherwise. Keep your Miracle dice to one side – this is your Miracle dice pool.\nPERFORMING AN ACT OF FAITH\nBefore making a dice roll for a model or unit from your army with the Acts of Faith ability, if you have one or more dice in your Miracle dice pool, that unit can perform an Act of Faith. If it does, select one of the dice from your Miracle dice pool to substitute that dice roll (if a roll involves more than one dice, e.g. a Charge roll or Battle-shock test, only a single dice can\nbe substituted). The dice that is being substituted is not rolled; instead the value of the selected Miracle dice is used as if it had been rolled (this counts as an unmodified dice roll of that value for all rules purposes). Each Miracle dice can only be selected for substitution once. Once all Miracle dice substitutions have been made, remove the chosen Miracle dice from your Miracle dice pool, and roll all remaining, unsubstituted dice that are a part of the dice roll. You can use Miracle dice when a unit performs an Act of Faith for any of the following types of dice roll:\n■ Advance roll\n■ Battle-shock test\n■ Charge roll\n■ Damage roll\n■ Hit roll\n■ Saving throw\n■ Wound roll'}, 'Deadly Demise D3': {'name': 'Deadly Demise D3', 'desc': 'This ability always takes the form Deadly Demise X. Each time a model in this unit is destroyed, after the units embarked within it (if any) have made their emergency disembark moves, roll one D6. On a 6, that model suffers a deadly demise; each unit within 6" of that model suffers a number of mortal wounds denoted by X (if this is a random number, roll separately for each unit within 6"). \nExample: An Impulsor with a unit of Intercessors embarked within it is destroyed by ranged attacks. First, any unresolved attacks made by the attacking unit are resolved. Then the Intercessors make an emergency disembark move. Then the roll is made for the Deadly Demise ability, and on a 6, that ability is resolved. Finally, the Impulsor is removed from the battlefield.'}, 'Symphonic Payload': {'name': 'Symphonic Payload', 'desc': 'This unit can re‑roll rolls to determine the A of a weapon.'}}, 'modelProfiles': {'Exorcist': {'m': '10"', 't': '10', 'sv': '3+', 'w': '11', 'ld': '7+', 'oc': '3', 'insv': '6+', 'name': 'Exorcist'}}, 'weapons': {'Heavy Bolter': {'range': '36"', 'a': '3', 'bsws': '3+', 's': '5', 'ap': '-1', 'd': '2', 'number': 1, 'abilities': 'Sustained Hits 1', 'shortAbilities': 'Sustained Hits 1', 'name': 'Heavy Bolter'}, 'Exorcist Missile Launcher': {'range': '36"', 'a': 'D6+2', 'bsws': '3+', 's': '10', 'ap': '-3', 'd': 'D6', 'number': 1, 'abilities': 'Indirect Fire', 'shortAbilities': 'Indirect Fire', 'name': 'Exorcist Missile Launcher'}, 'Armoured tracks': {'range': 'Melee', 'a': '3', 'bsws': '4+', 's': '6', 'ap': '0', 'd': '1', 'number': 1, 'abilities': '-', 'shortAbilities': '-', 'name': 