ssors embarked within it is destroyed by ranged attacks. First, any unresolved attacks made by the attacking unit are resolved. Then the Intercessors make an emergency disembark move. Then the roll is made for the Deadly Demise ability, and on a 6, that ability is resolved. Finally, the Impulsor is removed from the battlefield.'}}, 'modelProfiles': {'Immolator': {'m': '12"', 't': '10', 'sv': '3+', 'w': '11', 'ld': '7+', 'oc': '2', 'insv': '6+', 'name': 'Immolator'}}, 'weapons': {'Heavy Bolter': {'range': '36"', 'a': '3', 'bsws': '3+', 's': '5', 'ap': '-1', 'd': '2', 'number': 1, 'abilities': 'Sustained Hits 1', 'shortAbilities': 'Sustained Hits 1', 'name': 'Heavy Bolter'}, 'Immolation Flamers': {'range': '18"', 'a': '2D6', 'bsws': 'N/A', 's': '6', 'ap': '-1', 'd': '1', 'number': 1, 'abilities': 'Ignores Cover, Torrent', 'shortAbilities': 'Ignores Cover, Torrent', 'name': 'Immolation Flamers'}, 'Armoured tracks': {'range': 'Melee', 'a': '3', 'bsws': '4+', 's': '6', 'ap': '0', 'd': '1', 'number': 1, 'abilities': '-', 'shortAbilities': '-', 'name': 'Armoured tracks'}}, 'rules': [], 'unassignedWeapons': []}, 'y4s9c64': {'name': 'Sororitas Rhino', 'factionKeywords': ['Adepta Sororitas'], 'keywords': ['Dedicated Transport', 'Frame', 'Imperium', 'Smoke', 'Sororitas Rhino', 'Transport', 'Vehicle'], 'models': {'models': {'6a6ad6f390a72027864dc989': {'name': 'Sororitas Rhino', 'number': 1, 'abilities': ['Transport', 'Self Repair', 'Acts of Faith', 'Firing Deck 2', 'Deadly Demise D3'], 'weapons': [{'name': 'Hunter-killer missile', 'number': 1}, {'name': 'Storm bolter', 'number': 1}, {'name': 'Armoured tracks', 'number': 1}]}}, 'totalNumberOfModels': 1}, 'isSingleModel': True, 'uuid': 'y4s9c64', 'abilities': {'Transport': {'name': 'Transport', 'desc': 'This model has a transport capacity of 12 ADEPTA SORORITAS INFANTRY models. It cannot transport JUMP PACK models or the TRIUMPH OF SAINT KATHERINE.'}, 'Self Repair': {'name': 'Self Repair', 'desc': 'At the start of your Command phase, this model regains 1 lost wound.'}, 'Acts of Faith': {'name': 'Acts of Faith', 'desc': 'If your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, each unit from your army with this ability can perform one Act of Faith per phase. This is done using Miracle dice.\nGAINING MIRACLE DICE\nIf your Army Faction is Adepta Sororitas, you gain 1 Miracle dice:\n\nAt the start of each battle round.\nEach time an Adepta Sororitas unit from your army is destroyed.\n\nEach time you gain a Miracle dice, roll one D6. The number you roll is the value of that Miracle dice. This value cannot be changed or re-rolled, unless a rule specifically states otherwise. Keep your Miracle dice to one side – this is your Miracle dice pool.\nPERFORMING AN ACT OF FAITH\nBefore making a dice roll for a model or unit from your army with the Acts of Faith ability, if you have one or more dice in your Miracle dice pool, that unit can perform an Act of Faith. If it does, select one of the dice from your Miracle dice pool to substitute that dice roll (if a roll involves more than one dice, e.g. a Charge roll or Battle-shock test, only a single dice can\nbe substituted). The dice that is being substituted is not rolled; instead the value of the selected Miracle dice is used as if it had been rolled (this counts as an unmodified dice roll of that value for all rules purposes). Each Miracle dice can only be selected for substitution once. Once all Miracle dice substitutions have been made, remove the chosen Miracle dice from your Miracle dice pool, and roll all remaining, unsubstituted dice that are a part of the dice roll. You can use Miracle dice when a unit performs an Act of Faith for any of the following types of dice roll:\n■ Advance roll\n■ Battle-shock test\n■ Charge roll\n■ Damage roll\n■ Hit roll\n■ Saving throw\n■ Wound roll'}, 'Firing Deck 2': {'name': 'Firing Deck 2', 'desc': 'This ability always takes the form Firing Deck X. In your Shooting phase, each time this TRANSPORT is selected to shoot, if one or more units are embarked within it, resolve the following sequence: \n\nSelect up to X models embarked within this TRANSPORT (excluding models whose units have already been selected to shoot this phase). \nFor each selected model, select one of its ranged weapons (excluding [ONE SHOT] weapons). \nUntil this TRANSPORT has resolved all of its attacks, it has all of those selected weapons in addition to its other weapons. \nUntil the end of the turn, units embarked within this TRANSPORT are not eligible to shoot. \n'}, 'Deadly Demise D3': {'name': 'Deadly Demise D3', 'desc': 'This ability always takes the form Deadly Demise X. Each time a model in this unit is destroyed, after the units embarked within it (if any) have made their emergency disembark moves, roll one D6. On a 6, that model suffers a deadly demise; each unit within 6" of that model suffers a number of mortal wounds denoted by X (if this is a random number, roll separately for each unit within 6"). \nExample: An Impulsor with a unit of Intercessors embarked within it is destroyed by ranged attacks. First, any unresolved attacks made by the attacking unit are resolved. Then the Intercessors make an emergency disembark move. Then the roll is made for the Deadly Demise ability, and on a 6, that ability is resolved. Finally, the Impulsor is removed from the battlefield.'}}, 'modelProfiles': {'Sororitas Rhino': {'m': '12"', 't': '9', 'sv': '3+', 'w': '10', 'ld': '7+', 'oc': '2', 'insv': '6+', 'name': 'Sororitas Rhino'}}, 'weapons': {'Hunter-killer missile': {'range': '48"', 'a': '1', 'bsws': '2+', 's': '14', 'ap': '-3', 'd': 'D6', 'number': 1, 'abilities': 'One Shot', 'shortAbilities': 'One Shot', 'name': 'Hunter-killer missile'}, 'Storm bolter': {'range': '24"', 'a': '2', 'bsws': '3+', 's': '4', 'ap': '0', 'd': '1', 'number': 1, 'abilities': 'Rapid Fire 2', 'shortAbilities': 'Rapid Fire 2', 'name': 'Storm bolter'}, 'Armoured tracks': {'range': 'Melee', 'a': '3', 'bsws': '4+', 's': '6', 'ap': '0', 'd': '1', 'number': 1, 'abilities': '-', 'shortAbilities': '-', 'name': 'Armoured tracks'}}, 'rules': [], 'unassignedWeapons': []}}